# RAG lab — every variable this project reads, commented out.
#
# `src/raglab/tests/test_conventions.py` asserts this list against the code in
# both directions: a variable missing here is undiscoverable, and one lingering
# after the code stopped reading it is a lie. That second direction is what
# caught RAGLAB_URL trying to come across in the move — it belonged to the
# Node proxy of the system this lab was extracted from, and nothing here has
# a proxy.
#
# Copy to `.env` and uncomment what you need. The file is read without
# overriding anything already in the environment.

# ── the chat backend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 'ollama' | 'openrouter' | 'claude' | 'codex' | 'fake'. Local Ollama is the
# default: a judged run can make hundreds of model calls, so a default must never
# silently spend credit. An unknown value raises — there is no auto mode anywhere
# in this project. 'claude' and 'codex' run the CLI already installed and logged
# in on this machine, once per call, so they need no key at all.
#RAGLAB_LLM=ollama
# Empty resolves per backend (PROVIDER_MODELS), because a slug only means
# something to the backend that serves it.
#RAGLAB_MODEL=
# How hard a CLI backend thinks. claude takes low|medium|high|xhigh|max, codex
# takes low|medium|high|none, and a value the chosen one rejects is refused
# rather than sent — codex answers an unaccepted value with exit 0 and no text.
#RAGLAB_CLI_EFFORT=low
#RAGLAB_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# Only needed by the 'openrouter' backend and by the judged metrics.
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
#OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# ── embedding and reranking models ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Multilingual on purpose: the popular small models are English-only and score
# Farsi pairs as noise.
#RAGLAB_FASTEMBED_MODEL=sentence-transformers/paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2
#RAGLAB_CROSS_ENCODER=jinaai/jina-reranker-v2-base-multilingual

# ── where finished experiments are recorded ──────────────────────────────────
#RAGLAB_DB=databases/raglab.db

# ── where the corpora experiments ran on are kept ────────────────────────────
# Written by src/raglab/corpora/corpus_store.py and read when an archive is
# served. Each row has an id — the key an archived experiment joins on — and is
# unique by the fingerprint of what it holds, so one corpus is stored once
# however many experiments reference it, and editing a corpus adds a version
# rather than replacing the one an older archive names. Text as it was and
# nothing built from it — there is no index here and no vector store.
#RAGLAB_CORPORA_DB=databases/corpora.db

# ── where the widget's conversations are kept ────────────────────────────────
# A conversation log and nothing else: no metric, no run, no ledger row. The
# board never reads it and no ranking may.
#RAGLAB_WIDGET_DB=databases/widget.db

# ── where an imported dataset is written ─────────────────────────────────────
# The bundled samples in fixtures/corpus_groundtruth_datasets/ are read-only
# reference points; anything imported through the panel lands here, git-ignored,
# because an uploaded corpus is the uploader's material rather than this
# repository's.
#RAGLAB_DATASETS=.datasets

# ── the panel's LLM widget ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read only by the `src/raglab/agents/widget` package, the corner helper — the
# measured pipeline never reads these. The OpenRouter path (the two tool-using
# models) needs only OPENROUTER_API_KEY above; the LangSmith four are demanded
# only when LANGSMITH_TRACING is on, because they exist only to serve tracing.
# The default is openai/gpt-5-nano over OpenRouter, because a default must be a
# model that can actually run the tool loop — so the widget needs
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY (here, or typed into the panel's Settings card) and answers
# 502 naming the missing variable without one. The keyless way to answer with
# nothing set is to pick the claude or codex CLI in the model picker, which
# costs the tools: a CLI has no bind_tools and answers in one call. Caveat:
# LANGSMITH_TRACING=true is process-global, so a measured run in the same
# process would be traced too — scope it before trusting a run alongside it.
#LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
#LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT=https://api.smith.langchain.com
#LANGSMITH_PROJECT=raglab-widget
#LANGSMITH_TRACING=true

# ── third-party telemetry ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RAGAS phones home unless told not to. Set by the code, listed here because it
# is a variable this project sets in your environment.
#RAGAS_DO_NOT_TRACK=true

# Developer trace page at /dev/trace, unlocked by typing this value on the
# page; unset = the page is a 404.
# RAGLAB_DEV_KEY=
